@startuml
title Document workflows — grouped sequence overview



hide footbox

autonumber

skinparam shadowing false

skinparam sequence {

  ArrowColor #444444

  LifeLineBorderColor #777777

  LifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF

  ParticipantBorderColor #555555

  GroupBorderColor #777777

  GroupBackgroundColor #FAFAFA

  DividerBackgroundColor #F4F4F4

  DividerBorderColor #777777

}



actor "User" as user



box "Frontend" #EEE6FF

  boundary "Frontend" as frontend

end box

box "Backend"

  control "Upload API" as upload_api

end box



box "Restate Workflows" #E8F1FF

  control "New Document" as new_workflow

  control "Document Extraction" as extraction_workflow

  control "Fix Document" as fix_workflow

  control "Update Document" as update_workflow

end box



box "Restate Services" #FFF3D6

  control "Garage Pipeline" as garage_service

  control "GROBID Extraction Pipeline" as grobid_service

  control "TEI Conversion Pipeline" as parsing_service

  control "Artifact Store" as postgres_service

  control "TypeDB Pipeline" as typedb_service

  control "Vector Pipeline" as vector_service

end box



box "External Containers" #EDEDED

  database "Garage" as garage

  participant "GROBID" as grobid

  database "PostgreSQL" as postgres

  database "TypeDB" as typedb

  database "Qdrant" as qdrant

  participant "Embedding API" as embeddings

end box



legend bottom

  Restate retries non-terminal service failures.

  Selected failure outcomes are expanded below.

endlegend



== User Entry Points ==



alt Start a new document

  user -> frontend : Upload PDF

  frontend -> upload_api : Forward PDF bytes

  upload_api -> garage : Persist PDF

  alt PDF storage fails

    garage --> upload_api : Storage failure

    upload_api --> frontend : Reject upload before workflow start

    frontend --> user : Display upload error

  else PDF storage succeeds

    garage --> upload_api : PDF content hash

    upload_api -> new_workflow : Start workflow with PDF hash

  end

else Update a published document

  user -> frontend : Select a published document and edit its metadata

  frontend -> update_workflow : Submit PDF hash and manual overrides

else Repair a staged document

  user -> frontend : Select a pending repair case and edit its draft

  frontend -> fix_workflow : Submit case ID and manual overrides

end



== New Document Workflow ==



note over new_workflow

  This section expands the new-document entry shown above.

end note



note over upload_api, new_workflow

  The PDF is durable in Garage before Restate starts.
  The workflow request contains the PDF hash, not the PDF bytes.
  New Document verifies the stored PDF metadata and links it to the workflow.

end note

new_workflow -> extraction_workflow : Run document extraction using the PDF hash

alt Extraction pipeline succeeds

   group GROBID Extraction Pipeline

     extraction_workflow -> grobid_service : Request TEI extraction using the PDF hash

     grobid_service -> garage_service : Load the PDF by content hash

     garage_service -> garage : Read the PDF object

     garage --> garage_service : PDF bytes

     garage_service --> grobid_service : PDF bytes

     grobid_service -> grobid : Submit the PDF for TEI extraction

     grobid --> grobid_service : TEI XML

     grobid_service --> extraction_workflow : TEI XML and validation warnings

   end



   group TEI Conversion Pipeline

     extraction_workflow -> parsing_service : Convert TEI XML to document data

     parsing_service --> extraction_workflow : Converted document data and validation warnings

   end



   extraction_workflow --> new_workflow : Extracted document data and validation warnings

   note over extraction_workflow, postgres_service
     On success, Document Extraction stores the TEI XML and draft in PostgreSQL.
     Those persistence calls are not expanded in this fixed arrow layout.
   end note

   new_workflow -> update_workflow : Continue along the canonical publication path
   note over new_workflow, update_workflow
     This arrow shows shared publication responsibilities.
     New Document performs them directly and does not invoke Update Document.
   end note

else Terminal PDF loading, GROBID extraction, or TEI conversion failure

   note over garage_service, parsing_service

     The pipeline service that classifies a failure as terminal

     stages its failure record before propagating the error.

   end note

   extraction_workflow -> postgres_service : Stage the terminal failure for review

   postgres_service -> postgres : Persist the review case and failure artifact

   alt Failure staging fails

     postgres --> postgres_service : Persistence failure

     postgres_service --> extraction_workflow : Review case not persisted

     extraction_workflow --> frontend : Extraction workflow failed

     frontend --> user : Display extraction error

   else Failure record is stored

     postgres --> postgres_service : Review case stored

     postgres_service --> extraction_workflow : Failure record persisted

     extraction_workflow -> fix_workflow : Expose a pending repair case

   end

end



== Fix Document Workflow ==



note over fix_workflow

  This section expands the repair entry shown above

  and the pending case produced by a terminal pipeline failure.

end note



fix_workflow -> postgres_service : Load the pending review case and repair draft

postgres_service -> postgres : Read the review case and draft

alt Repair data retrieval fails

  postgres --> postgres_service : Retrieval failure

  postgres_service --> fix_workflow : Repair data unavailable

  fix_workflow --> frontend : Repair cannot continue; staged data remains stored

  frontend --> user : Display repair-loading error

else Repair data is available

  postgres --> postgres_service : Pending review case and draft

  postgres_service --> fix_workflow : Repair context

  fix_workflow --> frontend : Repair draft and canonical validation requirements

  frontend --> user : Display the editable repair draft

  loop Until the required canonical fields are supplied

   user -> frontend : Supply a title and at least one named contributor

  end

  note over user, frontend

   The frontend blocks submission while required canonical data is missing.

  end note

  frontend -> fix_workflow : Submit the case ID and manual overrides

  fix_workflow -> update_workflow : Continue with PDF hash, overrides, and review-case reference

end



== Update Document Workflow ==



note over update_workflow

  This section expands direct updates and the handoff from Fix Document.

  New Document performs the same publication responsibilities directly.

end note



update_workflow -> postgres_service : Load the source artifact and save the revised draft

postgres_service -> postgres : Read the source artifact and write the draft

alt Artifact preparation fails

  postgres --> postgres_service : Artifact preparation failure

  postgres_service --> update_workflow : Source unavailable or revised draft not persisted

  update_workflow --> frontend : Update workflow failed

  frontend --> user : Display artifact-preparation error

else Revised draft is stored

  postgres --> postgres_service : Source loaded and draft stored

  postgres_service --> update_workflow : Success



  update_workflow -> typedb_service : Publish the effective document data

  note right of update_workflow

   Update Document sends the effective new document and PDF hash.

   For an existing publication, it also sends the old document.

  end note



  typedb_service -> postgres_service : Depend on the artifact state loaded by Update Document

  postgres_service -> postgres : Read the draft and any published artifact

  note over postgres_service, postgres

   These arrows show a data dependency, not a direct service call.

   Update Document loads the artifacts before calling the TypeDB Pipeline.

  end note



  alt Required artifact state is unavailable

   postgres --> postgres_service : Retrieval failure

   postgres_service --> typedb_service : Retrieval failed

   typedb_service --> update_workflow : Publication cannot start

   update_workflow --> frontend : Draft stored but canonical publication incomplete

   frontend --> user : Display publication error

  else Required artifact state is available

   postgres --> postgres_service : Draft and any published artifact

   postgres_service --> typedb_service : Effective new document and optional old document

   typedb_service -> typedb : Insert canonical data or apply graph changes



   alt TypeDB publication fails

     typedb --> typedb_service : Publication failure

     typedb_service --> update_workflow : Canonical publication failed

     update_workflow --> frontend : Draft stored but canonical publication incomplete

     frontend --> user : Display TypeDB publication error

   else Canonical publication succeeds

     typedb --> typedb_service : Success

     update_workflow -> vector_service : Publish changed effective passages

     vector_service -> embeddings : Embed added or changed passage text

     embeddings --> vector_service : Embedding vectors

     vector_service -> qdrant : Delete stale points and upsert new vectors

     qdrant --> vector_service : Awaited update completed

     note over typedb_service, postgres_service
       This block shows post-publication finalization.
       Update Document calls the Artifact Store after TypeDB returns.
     end note



     loop Retry transient finalization failures

       typedb_service -> postgres_service : Finalize the published artifact and repair case

       postgres_service -> postgres : Store the published artifact and resolve the repair case

       alt Finalization fails

         postgres --> postgres_service : Failure

         postgres_service --> typedb_service : Retryable failure

       else Finalization succeeds

         postgres --> postgres_service : Success

         postgres_service --> typedb_service : Success

       end

     end



     typedb_service --> update_workflow : Success

     update_workflow --> frontend : Publication completed

     frontend --> user : Document ready

   end

  end

end
@enduml
